It stops polling on SIGTERM/SIGINT, drains the active job within a deadline, and deletes messages only after successful processing. Failed or interrupted messages become available after their visibility timeout. SQS can deliver duplicates, so the job handler must make effects idempotent. [SQS delivery and visibility semantics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-visibility-timeout.html)

